  "note": "Triennial election of the Ballyclare Urban Council, poll due 18 May 1949. Only six nominations were received for the nine seats, so six were returned unopposed and the three remaining seats were filled by co-option (Larne Times, 5 May 1949, p. 6; Belfast News-Letter, 31 May 1949, p. 4). No poll: four retiring members did not seek nomination and only six candidates came forward for nine seats; the three vacant seats were filled by co-option at the annual meeting. Returned unopposed."
